Z||000000||colts60||11-27-2000||03:46 PM||||On my 1984, both rear upper inner steel fender panels are rusted out where the steel is curved to support the plastic inner fender. Steel patches on flat surfaces are no problem, but to bend curved patches is nearly impossible. Has anyone made the same repair? Are replacement panels available?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-27-2000||04:35 PM||||The only substantial fix is to replace the support member.  If that has rusted through, more than likely there is other substantial rust damage that hasn't been located yet.  Many people just part out the car when rust is present, unless you want to invest in some expensive repairs.  Unfortunatly an 84 Fiero is the least valuable Fiero except for the Pace car, so spending lots of money on a rusted Fiero is not cost effective.<P>Many of the Fiero recyclers may have parts that can be used as replacements.  Check with Ed Parks, Bob Steiger or MrFiero on the forum.  These people do a lot with Fieros.||||reg||9
